# Optional. With neither of these set, the workspace runs exactly as it always
# has — locally, in your browser, with no account and no network — and the
# "Sign in to sync" control simply does not appear.
#
# Setting them adds one thing: a signed-in learner's course progress,
# prediction record, working prompt and saved designs are also kept in
# Supabase, so they follow them to another machine.
#
# Copy to `.env` (git-ignored) and fill in from your Supabase project:
#   Dashboard → Project Settings → API

VITE_SUPABASE_URL=https://your-project.supabase.co

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# THE ANON / PUBLISHABLE KEY. NOT THE SERVICE ROLE KEY.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# Every VITE_* variable is compiled into the JavaScript bundle at build time.
# It is not a secret: anyone who loads the page can read it.
#
# That is fine for the anon key, which carries no authority of its own —
# Row Level Security (see supabase/migrations/) decides what the signed-in
# user may touch.
#
# It is catastrophic for the service role key, which bypasses RLS entirely.
# Putting one here hands every visitor full read and write access to your
# database. The app checks for this at boot and refuses to start the client,
# but the real protection is not doing it.
VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=your-anon-publishable-key
